---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RankineCycle from '../components/RankineCycle.svelte';
import RankineEquations from '../components/RankineEquations.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="H2O Rankine">
  <section class="rankine-hero">
    <div class="rankine-align">
      <div class="title-row">
        <svg class="molecule" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 40 30"><defs><pattern id="mol-knob-tex" patternUnits="objectBoundingBox" patternContentUnits="objectBoundingBox" width="1" height="1"><image href="/buttons/knob-silver.png" x="0" y="0" width="1" height="1" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"/></pattern></defs><line class="mol-bond" x1="20" y1="14" x2="8" y2="24"/><line class="mol-bond" x1="20" y1="14" x2="32" y2="24"/><circle class="mol-h" cx="8" cy="24" r="4"/><circle class="mol-h" cx="32" cy="24" r="4"/><circle class="mol-o" cx="20" cy="14" r="7"/><circle class="mol-h-tint" cx="8" cy="24" r="4"/><circle class="mol-h-tint" cx="32" cy="24" r="4"/><circle class="mol-o-tint" cx="20" cy="14" r="7"/><text class="mol-label mol-label-h" x="8" y="24">H</text><text class="mol-label mol-label-h" x="32" y="24">H</text><text class="mol-label mol-label-o" x="20" y="14">O</text></svg>
        <h2 class="page-title">Supercritical H<sub>2</sub>O Reheat Regenerative Rankine Cycle</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="scroll-hint">
        <span>Scroll for simulator</span>
        <svg class="scroll-hint-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true">
          <polyline points="3,6 8,11 13,6" />
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="cycle-intro">
        <p>
          Ah, the good old Rankine cycle. It is used extensively in thermal power stations,
          like nuclear fission, coal, oil, combined-cycle natural gas, and even
          concentrated solar power (CSP). Often boiled down to (pun not intended) boiling water
          to spin a turbine, the simplest form of the Rankine cycle is just four components
          in a loop: [1] a boiler adds heat at constant pressure, [2] a turbine expands the resulting steam
          to produce work, [3] a condenser rejects heat at constant pressure back to
          saturated liquid, and [4] a pump raises the liquid back to boiler
          pressure. Below you will find that an applied Rankine cycle is far from simple.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Supercritical</strong> means the boiler pressure is pushed
          above water's critical pressure of 22.064 MPa. Above this pressure, there is no separate liquid and
          vapor phase and no flat constant-temperature plateau. This allows the boiler to add heat at a higher average
          temperature than a subcritical boiler. Supercritical Rankine
          cycles have been employed in coal plants for about as long as nuclear fission
          has been on the grid (the 1950s), however nuclear fission plants have never used supercritical
          Rankine cycles due to relatively low reactor operating temperatures and stress corrosion cracking concerns.
          Fusion may be a different story.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Reheat</strong> means the steam isn't expanded from boiler
          pressure all the way down to condenser pressure in one turbine. Expansion is split
          into stages with reheating. After the HP turbine drops the pressure partway,
          the steam runs back through a reheater and picks up more heat before
          continuing through the IP and LP turbines. This keeps the LP
          turbine's exhaust quality from getting too low, which would erode its blades. The second high-temperature heat-addition step also raises efficiency and output.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Regenerative</strong> means some of the steam is bled off the
          turbines at several pressures and used to preheat the feedwater before reaching the boiler. The model below
          accomplishes this through six closed feedwater heaters and one deaerator. Without regeneration, relatively cold
          water straight out of the condenser would be dumped directly into the steam generator, a large and wasteful
          temperature mismatch. We hate that. Preheating the feedwater first means the boiler only must add heat over a smaller, hotter temperature range, reducing entropy generation and greatly
          improving efficiency.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="hero-bottom-bar"></div>
  <div class="rankine-align diagram-title-row">
    <h3 class="page-title">Supercritical H<sub>2</sub>O Reheat Regenerative Rankine Cycle Diagram</h3>
  </div>
  <div class="page-breakout">
    <img class="cycle-diagram diagram-rankine" src="/diagrams/fusion-rankine.png" alt="Process flow diagram of the supercritical reheat regenerative Rankine cycle balance of plant" width="2457" height="1052" />
  </div>
  <p class="rankine-align diagram-credit">
    Cycle layout adapted from
    Colliva, F.; Ciurluini, C.; Iaboni, A.; Centomani, G.V.; Trotta, A.; Giannetti, F.
    "Analysis of Power Conversion System Options for ARC-like Tokamak Fusion Reactor
    Balance of Plant." <em>Sustainability</em> <strong>2024</strong>, <em>16</em>, 7480. <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/su16177480" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">doi.org/10.3390/su16177480</a>
  </p>
  <div class="hero-bottom-bar sim-intro-bar"></div>
  <div class="rankine-align sim-intro">
    <h3 class="page-title">Introducing the Simulator</h3>
    <p>
      Below is a live model of the cycle shown above. Move any slider and the
      whole system re-solves from scratch using IAPWS-95 steam properties
      through CoolProp. See the "Modeling Details" section below the simulator
      to learn more about the equations the simulator uses.
    </p>
    <p>
      Both the left and the right sides scroll independently.
      On the left, you will find adjustable sliders categorized within different dropdown
      menus. This is your side to tinker. On the right, you will find a T-s diagram of the
      cycle, along with many indicators. Some may glow red if taken out of recommended operating
      conditions. Scroll down on the right to see the temperature, pressure, specific enthalpy, specific
      entropy, and mass flow rate of each state.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="try-things">
    <svg class="try-things-border" aria-hidden="true">
      <polygon />
    </svg>
    <h4 class="sim-intro-subhead">Try these things!</h4>
    <ul class="sim-tips">
      <li>
        Open the "Steam Conditions" dropdown.
        Drop the steam generator outlet pressure (P<sub>1</sub>) below 22 MPa. What happens to the curve? Is the cycle still supercritical?
      </li>
      <li>
        Open the "Extraction Pressures and Feedwater Heating" dropdown.
        Bypass all feedwater heating. What happens to First and Second Law efficiency?
        What about LP exhaust quality?
      </li>
      <li>
        Open the "Isentropic Efficiencies" dropdown and adjust turbine efficiencies.
        Observe how the shape of the cycle curve changes.
      </li>
      <li>
        Here's an interesting one:
        Open the "Cooling / Environment" dropdown. Push the ambient temperature up. What happens to condenser
        pressure? Do First Law and Second Law efficiency change by the same amount, or even
        in the same direction? Why?
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="simulator-box chamfer-panel chamfer-all">
    <!-- wrapper needed: astro-island is display:contents, chamfer-panel's z-index promotion no-ops without it -->
    <div><RankineCycle client:load /></div>
  </div>
  <RankineEquations />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // chamfered border, drawn once when "Try these things!" scrolls into view,
  // then left drawn - re-bound on astro:page-load since ClientRouter swaps the
  // DOM without a full reload.
  //
  // The polygon is sized in real pixels (not a stretched 0-100 viewBox) because
  // a non-square box scaled non-uniformly distorts vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke
  // at the corners - sizing it to the box's actual dimensions avoids that.
  const CHAMFER = 14; // px, matches --chamfer in global.css

  function sizeTryThingsBorder() {
    const wrap = document.querySelector('.try-things');
    const svg = wrap?.querySelector('.try-things-border');
    const poly = svg?.querySelector('polygon');
    if (!wrap || !svg || !poly) return;
    const w = wrap.clientWidth, h = wrap.clientHeight;
    if (!w || !h) return;
    const cf = Math.min(CHAMFER, w / 2, h / 2);
    svg.setAttribute('viewBox', `0 0 ${w} ${h}`);
    poly.setAttribute('points', [
      [cf, 0], [w - cf, 0], [w, cf], [w, h - cf],
      [w - cf, h], [cf, h], [0, h - cf], [0, cf],
    ].map(p => p.join(',')).join(' '));
    poly.setAttribute('pathLength', '1');
  }

  function initTryThingsBorder() {
    const el = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.try-things');
    if (!el) return;
    sizeTryThingsBorder();
    if (!el.dataset.observed) {
      el.dataset.observed = 'true';
      new ResizeObserver(sizeTryThingsBorder).observe(el);
      if (!el.classList.contains('in-view')) {
        const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
          for (const entry of entries) {
            if (entry.isIntersecting) {
              el.classList.add('in-view');
              io.unobserve(el);
            }
          }
        }, { threshold: 0.3 });
        io.observe(el);
      }
    }
  }
  initTryThingsBorder();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initTryThingsBorder);
</script>

<style>
  /* wider cap than the other cycle pages: this plant has ~2x the equipment */
  .diagram-rankine { max-width: 1560px; }

  /* matches simulator-box's content width (1100px box - 72px padding) */
  .rankine-align {
    max-width: 1028px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* full-bleed teal-fade hero, same recipe as the homepage */
  .rankine-hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: -24px -24px 0;
    padding: 40px max(24px, calc(50vw - 640px)) 32px;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(53, 214, 180, 0.11), rgba(53, 214, 180, 0) 88%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 42%),
      linear-gradient(163deg, var(--steel-300), var(--steel-500) 85%);
    background-blend-mode: normal;
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
  }

  /* single large decorative H2O molecule flanking the title, solid filled atoms labeled H/O */
  /* title-row is just a positioning anchor: the molecule is absolutely
     positioned into the left margin so it never shifts the title text,
     which stays flush with the same left edge as the rest of the page. */
  .title-row {
    position: relative;
  }
  /* this page's own identity gets a bigger title than section headings like "Cycle Diagram" */
  .title-row .page-title {
    font-size: 30px;
  }
  .molecule {
    position: absolute;
    right: 100%;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    margin-right: 14px;
    width: 112px;
    height: auto;
    opacity: 0.95;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1220px) {
    .molecule { display: none; }
  }
  .molecule .mol-bond { stroke: var(--steel-900); stroke-width: 2.5; stroke-linecap: round; }
  .molecule .mol-h { fill: url(#mol-knob-tex); }
  .molecule .mol-o { fill: url(#mol-knob-tex); }
  /* same teal wash the slider thumbs lay over their knob texture, so the atoms read as the site's metal, not raw chrome */
  .molecule .mol-h-tint { fill: var(--teal); opacity: 0.5; pointer-events: none; }
  .molecule .mol-o-tint { fill: var(--teal-dim); opacity: 0.6; pointer-events: none; }
  .molecule .mol-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    fill: #ffffff;
    text-anchor: middle;
    dominant-baseline: central;
  }
  .molecule .mol-label-o { font-size: 7.5px; }
  .molecule .mol-label-h { font-size: 5px; }

  .scroll-hint {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    margin: 2px 0 18px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--teal-dim);
  }
  .scroll-hint-arrow {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--teal-dim);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .cycle-intro {
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .cycle-intro p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .cycle-intro p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .cycle-intro strong { color: var(--paper); font-weight: 700; }

  /* brushed-metal strip matching the nav bar's chamfer-panel rim weight */
  .hero-bottom-bar {
    height: 16px;
    margin: 0 -24px;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35), transparent 40%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--steel-650), var(--steel-800)),
      var(--aluminum);
    background-repeat: no-repeat, no-repeat, no-repeat;
    background-size: 100% 100%, 100% 100%, cover;
    background-position: center, center, center;
    background-blend-mode: normal, overlay, normal;
    border-top: 1.5px solid var(--steel-900);
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--steel-900);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5), inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
  }

  /* spacing so the title isn't flush against the bar above */
  .diagram-title-row {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .diagram-credit {
    margin: 4px auto 28px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .diagram-credit em { font-style: italic; }
  .diagram-credit a {
    color: var(--teal-dim);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .diagram-credit a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .sim-intro { margin-top: 32px; }
  .sim-intro .page-title { margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .sim-intro p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .sim-intro p:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }
  /* teal border draws itself once, the first time this scrolls into view (see
     the script below), then stays put - unlike the homepage's spinning BoP
     ring, which never stops */
  .try-things {
    position: relative;
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 22px auto 32px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
  .try-things-border {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
    overflow: visible;
  }
  .try-things-border polygon {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--teal);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 1px;
    stroke-dashoffset: 1px;
  }
  .try-things.in-view .try-things-border polygon {
    animation: try-things-draw 2.4s ease-out 0.4s forwards;
  }
  @keyframes try-things-draw {
    to { stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .try-things-border polygon { stroke-dashoffset: 0; animation: none; }
  }
  .try-things .sim-intro-subhead { margin-top: 0; }

  .sim-intro-subhead {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--paper);
    margin: 22px 0 10px;
  }
  .sim-tips {
    list-style: disc;
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 22px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .sim-tips li {
    display: list-item;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .sim-tips li::marker { color: var(--teal-dim); }
  .sim-tips sub { font-weight: 700; }
</style>
